    notes: "Emo is an extension of the Emperor's emotional architecture rather than a traditional beast. It does not exist independently — it is Mira's function as conduit given form. Adore and Malice are a later, distinct addition — not Mira's emotions read through Irane, but Irane's own stored emotion, accumulated during Minia's week-long torture and first released through Constraint at the moment of his rescue. Malice resurfaced within hours of the reincarnation, in Facility Arc Part 5.5 ('Kazemi Soul!') — this time not released through a blade but manifesting directly as a massive Hatred-Wolf, Irane's post-reincarnation self-loathing turned inward and, because the core generating it lives in Mira, striking at her rather than any outside target. The attack produced a new Art on the spot, Kazemi's Will: Concentrated Hatred, before Dima and then Aphexia intervened to separate and ground both Emo and the newly-manifested Dima. Emo cycled back down through Grief into Love/Adore only once Irane worked through the reincarnation-vs-rebirth distinction with Hope by the tree afterward — the crisis settling, not resolving; the self-hatred that produced Malice in the first place remained. Enari's child — all beasts in the Kazemi and Valariyan systems trace their origin to Enari, the Primordial Dragon of Infinity, who is the father-source of every beast through his Primordial essence via Iris.",
